  "currency": "USD",
  "note": [
    "Prices are per million tokens for first-party APIs. This catalog ships only",
    "entries the maintainers can source; a model that is not listed gets no cost",
    "metric rather than a guessed one. Supply your own numbers with a project",
    "pricing file (pricing.path) or per-model `card:` overrides, and always",
    "verify against your provider's current price list before making a decision",
    "on cost.",
    "",
    "`privacy` is deliberately empty for real models: whether a DPA is in place,",
    "whether training opt-out applies, and whether zero-data-retention is enabled",
    "are properties of YOUR contract and platform, not of the model. Declare them",
    "in your project's pricing file. The one exception is a documented model-level",
    "restriction, recorded below as an explicit false.",
    "",
    "Every figure here is the published pay-as-you-go LIST price for the model's",
    "own first-party API, in USD per million tokens, as of the `as_of` date. It is",
    "not your price. Volume and committed-use discounts, the batch and cached-token",
    "rates, and resale through Bedrock / Vertex / OpenRouter all differ, and vendors",
    "reprice often — several models below have been repriced more than once inside a",
    "year. Verify against the provider's current price list before you make a",
    "purchasing decision on these numbers.",
    "",
    "Models whose current list price could not be confirmed are absent on purpose.",
    "Absent means no cost metric, which is the honest answer; a plausible-looking",
    "guess would quietly corrupt the comparison it was added to help."
  ],
